(3833907, 536024, 25095, '<td valign="top">Ok appears to be a single light bulb lighting from the top, which by the way gives it a very cool (pun not really intended) effect.  I''m guessing that the object isn''t normally blue and was either lit this way or colors were adjusted so I would have to say...I have no clue what the heck it is :).  Thye appear to be bent tubular items but that''s all I got.<br/> <br/>I like your placement within the image, the black and blue really work well together.  Can''t wait to see what it really is.</td>', 'Ok appears to be a single light bulb lighting from the top, which by the way gives it a very cool (pun not really intended) effect.  I''m guessing that the object isn''t normally blue and was either lit this way or colors were adjusted so I would have to say...I have no clue what the heck it is :).  Thye appear to be bent tubular items but that''s all I got. I like your placement within the image, the black and blue really work well together.  Can''t wait to see what it really is.', '2007-06-25 21:58:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(3833914, 536426, 25095, '<td valign="top">Not too difficult to see what it is but that doesn''t detract from the image.  Your DOF really makes for a cool image.  I like the subtle purples and greens in the image and the black just adds to it. Interesting.</td>', 'Not too difficult to see what it is but that doesn''t detract from the image.  Your DOF really makes for a cool image.  I like the subtle purples and greens in the image and the black just adds to it. Interesting.', '2007-06-25 22:00:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3833925, 539520, 25095, '<td valign="top">Well the coil has certainly rubbed there a lot as it has caused slight grooves but the rust would make me guess it hasn''t been used lately...crap I have no clue what it is!  All I know is a coil around another piece of metal, can''t think of what it would be used for.  I do however know I like your lighting and depth of field.  Your slightly gradient background is very nice and follows the tones on the inside of the coils.  Nice image.</td>', 'Well the coil has certainly rubbed there a lot as it has caused slight grooves but the rust would make me guess it hasn''t been used lately...crap I have no clue what it is!  All I know is a coil around another piece of metal, can''t think of what it would be used for.  I do however know I like your lighting and depth of field.  Your slightly gradient background is very nice and follows the tones on the inside of the coils.  Nice image.', '2007-06-25 22:04:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3833929, 535902, 25095, '<td valign="top">Someone''s been playing with their kid''s play-dough kit.  Nice mix of colors but I can''t really find a nice sharp place for my eyes, it all seems a bit out of focus.</td>', 'Someone''s been playing with their kid''s play-dough kit.  Nice mix of colors but I can''t really find a nice sharp place for my eyes, it all seems a bit out of focus.', '2007-06-25 22:06:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3833938, 538546, 25095, '<td valign="top">cool plant(?)!  The title loaded first and I was expecting tons of yellow and was surprised with the inital purple that came up.  You have a very nice level of colors here that play well together.  The white stuff almost seems like clouds, adding to the effect.  Nice job.</td>', 'cool plant(?)!  The title loaded first and I was expecting tons of yellow and was surprised with the inital purple that came up.  You have a very nice level of colors here that play well together.  The white stuff almost seems like clouds, adding to the effect.  Nice job.', '2007-06-25 22:08:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3833956, 539768, 25095, '<td valign="top">I have to admit that I think without your border this image would lose a lot of it''s punch.  I like the purples (pink, magenta, whatever it is) and blacks that make up the flower so the border only adds to it.  The bit of white adds a nice contrast while not over powering the image. Very neat pattern...oh, just came to me, I would love to see a single yellow bee sitting up on it, don''t suppose you could go catch one and put him on there could ya? lol  Very nice image.</td>', 'I have to admit that I think without your border this image would lose a lot of it''s punch.  I like the purples (pink, magenta, whatever it is) and blacks that make up the flower so the border only adds to it.  The bit of white adds a nice contrast while not over powering the image. Very neat pattern...oh, just came to me, I would love to see a single yellow bee sitting up on it, don''t suppose you could go catch one and put him on there could ya? lol  Very nice image.', '2007-06-25 22:12:18.000000', NULL, 1),
