(3840373, 537511, 18367, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=537485" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6519/thumb/537485.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6519/thumb/537485.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6519/thumb/537485.jpg"/></a>I do hope you won''t mind... I took the liberty of fixing your link.<br/> <br/>Very nice set up...Now I understand what it is that you were referring to.  I don''t do much sewing and had no idea what "Plastic Press Studs" are, but I do now. <br/> <br/>Thanks for sharing.<br/> <br/>Ray<br/> <br/></td>', 'I do hope you won''t mind... I took the liberty of fixing your link. Very nice set up...Now I understand what it is that you were referring to.  I don''t do much sewing and had no idea what "Plastic Press Studs" are, but I do now.  Thanks for sharing. Ray ', '2007-06-27 05:53:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3840375, 539150, 37858, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the kind comments.  Most of you had no trouble figuring out what I photographed.  The references to Sherpet''s fine work are high praise...and to be truthful, she is the inspiration for this image.</td>', 'Thanks for all the kind comments.  Most of you had no trouble figuring out what I photographed.  The references to Sherpet''s fine work are high praise...and to be truthful, she is the inspiration for this image.', '2007-06-27 05:54:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3840377, 539824, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by akinser:</b></div><hr/><i> Amazing shot! but the song is about red balloons... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually it''s not. Someone can correct me if I''m wrong but "luftballon" in German simply means "balloon". When the song was translated into English the word red was added just so the flow of the song remained the same. Regardless, it''s a protest song about bombs and doomsday during the cold war days. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-27 09:18:33.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by akinser: Amazing shot! but the song is about red balloons...   Actually it''s not. Someone can correct me if I''m wrong but "luftballon" in German simply means "balloon". When the song was translated into English the word red was added just so the flow of the song remained the same. Regardless, it''s a protest song about bombs and doomsday during the cold war days. ', '2007-06-27 05:54:31.000000', '2007-06-27 10:18:33.000000', 0),
