(3841007, 535686, 79861, '<td valign="top">Alrighty, Thank you all for the comments.<br/> <br/>I recently bought one of those illegal to own tiny baby turtles and currently keep him in this large plastic tank thats semi shallow.  I went outside and grabbed some bricks and scrubbed them clean and placed them i nthe tank.  Since the bricks were bone dry and only got damp when i cleaned them, when i placed them in hte water they began to slowly soak water from the tank.  This resulted in the creation of very super tiny bubbles that aligned perfectly to one another, the thing in the background is the top leaf to a baby bok choy leaf that was approx 2 inches in length.  So if you can use that for comparison to size of the bubbles.</td>', 'Alrighty, Thank you all for the comments. I recently bought one of those illegal to own tiny baby turtles and currently keep him in this large plastic tank thats semi shallow.  I went outside and grabbed some bricks and scrubbed them clean and placed them i nthe tank.  Since the bricks were bone dry and only got damp when i cleaned them, when i placed them in hte water they began to slowly soak water from the tank.  This resulted in the creation of very super tiny bubbles that aligned perfectly to one another, the thing in the background is the top leaf to a baby bok choy leaf that was approx 2 inches in length.  So if you can use that for comparison to size of the bubbles.', '2007-06-27 10:16:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3841011, 535686, 79861, '<td valign="top">Oh and btw, this was not taken with my 10d, this was taken with a canon digital elph 550 :)</td>', 'Oh and btw, this was not taken with my 10d, this was taken with a canon digital elph 550 :)', '2007-06-27 10:17:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3841076, 538671, 66267, '<td valign="top">For you, klynn, I''ll tell. I was really cheesed off about the score, but ill give away my secret anyway.<br/> <br/>Quite a few of you got the answer... sort of.<br/> <br/>It is paper, and it''s tied up on string in front of my monitor. Unfortunately, in basic editing i had to get rid of the string with heavy applications of levels, so I couldn''t get the three dimensional appearance that i was hoping for. All the levels and contrast made it appear all three paper cutouts were in focus, which is not the case.<br/> <br/>So congratulations to Sheryll for getting the right answer. And for those who guessed paper, you can be the runners up. :P</td>', 'For you, klynn, I''ll tell. I was really cheesed off about the score, but ill give away my secret anyway. Quite a few of you got the answer... sort of. It is paper, and it''s tied up on string in front of my monitor. Unfortunately, in basic editing i had to get rid of the string with heavy applications of levels, so I couldn''t get the three dimensional appearance that i was hoping for. All the levels and contrast made it appear all three paper cutouts were in focus, which is not the case. So congratulations to Sheryll for getting the right answer. And for those who guessed paper, you can be the runners up. :P', '2007-06-27 10:30:39.000000', NULL, 0),
